    "label": {
      "en": "Employee PRSI Class A- Rate 2"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tscee_prsiA_rate2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This constant is the withdrawal (taper) rate of one-sixth applied to the PRSI Class A credit as earnings rise above the credit's starting threshold. It is used as the Withdraw_Rate parameter of the BenCalc function in tscee_ie labelled 'PRSI Class A: credit (per month in work)', reducing the €12 maximum credit (tscee_prsiA_amt) by one-sixth of the amount by which weekly earnings exceed the threshold (tscee_prsiA_thres1). This directly matches the country report's description of the tapered PRSI credit introduced in 2016, which equals €12 less one-sixth of weekly earnings above €352.01."
    },
